    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d326">

                <pb facs="0497" n="403" sameAs="frus:frus1896/pg403"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Adee to Baron Fava.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1896-08-28"><hi rendition="#italic">August 28,
                        1896</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 148.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: I hasten to send you, in accordance
                    with the promise heretofore made to you by Acting Secretary Rockhill, the
                    awaited report of the recent lynching of certain persons, apparently of Italian
                    nationality, at Hahnville, La., which has just reached the Department from his
                    excellency the governor of Louisiana.</p>
                <p>I need do no more at this moment than invite your attention to the statement of
                    the local judge and district attorney, who join in making the report in
                    question, that while the results of the investigation so far are very
                    unsatisfactory, no effort will be spared to find the guilty parties.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alvey A. Adee</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d326-a1.xml" xpointer="d326-a1"/>
